Permission to Evaluate
----------------------

ZLAR Inc. and Vincent Nijjar give anyone permission to download this source and
run it on their own computers, including with the help of AI tools, solely to
study and evaluate it. For that purpose you may also change your own local copy.
Offering changes back to ZLAR, for example as a pull request to this repository,
is also permitted.

This permission does not extend to using the source in production or for any
other purpose, providing it as a service, distributing it or any changed version
of it, or creating derivative works for any purpose other than evaluation. Those
require separate written permission. This permission may be withdrawn for future
use by updating this notice.

Permission to Test and Publish
------------------------------

Anyone may test ZLAR, attack it, measure it, and publish what they find,
including benchmarks, weaknesses and ways to break it, without asking first.

When publishing a finding, you may include the short excerpts of ZLAR's source,
and the small changes to it, that are needed to show or reproduce the finding.
This permission does not cover publishing or distributing the source as a whole
or in substantial part.

It covers your own copies and systems you are authorized to test. It does not
authorize attacking anyone else's systems, or ZLAR's website, accounts or
infrastructure.

We ask, but do not require, that you tell us privately before publishing a way
to break ZLAR, so it can be fixed first. See SECURITY.md.

Findings published under this permission stay publishable even if this notice
changes later.

